[1m[38;2;0;191;255mPURPOSE[0m
[38;5;252mJørgen 2026-11-19 08:55Z: attach a request to a piece of the text in a mark mode, so the AI knows exactly what it is about; questions today look like         [39m
[38;5;252macceptance                                                                                                                                                    [39m
[38;5;252mcriteria. 09:05Z (answer 1 on this task): threads inside the ticket would bloat it, and the conversation must not become the thing. The ticket must stay      [39m
[38;5;252mcrisp: clarity comes from boiling text down to its essence. The messy part goes to a separate, suitably named history file in the task's files (provenance,   [39m
[38;5;252mchat history) that grows by appending.                                                                                                                        [39m

[1m[38;2;0;191;255mPRINCIPLE[0m
[38;5;252mTicket = working document, short and current. History = append-only provenance file, linked from the ticket, never needed to understand the ticket. Marks are [39m
[38;5;252mplain text in the field they are about, so git, grep, any editor and any agent see them. Resolving a mark means changing the ticket, not adding to it. The    [39m
[38;5;252magent instruction: lead with clarity in the ticket, answer and act on marks, post new questions as marks, move the dialogue to history. Reuse an existing     [39m
[38;5;252mmarkup convention for the sigil if one fits. Either side may resolve a mark (Jørgen 09:05Z): the person accepts, approves or asks for something else; the     [39m
[38;5;252magent judges by the ticket whether the mark is answered. Both use judgment, and either can initiate a resolve for clarity. Anchors (Jørgen 09:06Z): a mark may[39m
[38;5;252msit on anything in the ticket's markdown, or point into an attachment by name plus line or section ('in mock-100x30.txt, line 12'); the attachment itself is  [39m
[38;5;252mnot edited. Dialogue never enters the ticket; the history may be split per thing discussed.                                                                   [39m

[1m[38;2;0;191;255mGOAL[0m
[38;5;252mThe ticket stays the crisp working document. A person or agent marks a piece of a task's text with a comment, question or request that sits inline in the     [39m
[38;5;252mtext, visible as text, with a recognizable sigil. The agent picks marks up, acts or answers, and resolves each by rewriting the ticket text to the clarified  [39m
[38;5;252mresult and removing the mark. The dialogue that led there (the mark, replies, who and when) is appended to a history file attached to the task, never kept in [39m
[38;5;252mthe ticket.                                                                                                                                                   [39m

